#descr "Corellon Larethian, whose titles included Creator of the Elves and the Protector, was the patron god of all elvenkind. He governed those things which are held in the highest esteem among the Tel'Quessir - magic, music, arts, crafts, poetry, and warfare. He approved of those who killed orcs and the followers of Lolth, blessed those who aided others, and was angered at any who defiled the dead or fled from their foes. Elves believed that they were destined for reincarnation through Corellon's divine essence, living again and again until they reached their final goal of self-perfection. Corellon, alongside Sehanine Moonbow, was the souls' guide towards that perfected state. 

Corellon watched over the elven race as a guardian. It has, however, been nearly 1,000 years since Corellon engaged in world-shaping events on Faerun. Some time before 714 DR, before the fall of Cormanthor, elves wearied of competing with humans over land and wanted land for themselves free of encroaching human expansion. Under Corellon, the Seldarine started the Retreat, a mystical compulsion felt by elves to abandon their lands for the hidden island of Evermeet. Most of Corellon's followers answered the call and left Faerûn. 

Former husband to Araushnee (later known as Lolth) and father of their two children, Vhaeraun and Eilistraee, Corellon has a colorful past. His battles against the orc god, Gruumsh, were legendary. His wife's betrayal nearly gave Gruumsh the advantage he needed to kill the elven god. Sehanine Moonbow saved his life, and as the elven creation myth tells, Corellons blood mixed with Sehanine's tears and the elven race was spawned. Upon reaching supposed safety, the two were then ambushed by Malar and barely survived. Araushnee became known as the Spider Queen, and the rest is a long but worthwhile read.

