#descr "Demogorgon was the demon lord and lesser deity of domination and the draining of energy. He was the embodiment of madness and destruction and sought to drag all down into the infinite depths of the Abyss. He was known by many names: called the Imprisoned One by the followers of Helm, Siosivash by the yuan-ti, Leemooggoogoon the Deep Father by the kuo-toa, and Ahmon-Ibor the Sibilant Beast by the troglodytes.

The first tanar'ri, formed from mortals' ancient fears, even his chosen race, the ixitxachitl, dared not speak his name aloud. Inspiring fear in even other demon lords, his self-proclaimed title of Prince of Demons was won by virtue of power and influence - many demons challenged it, but none could defeat Demogorgon and claim it.

Demogorgon preferred to avoid direct conflict, instead using magic to help his servants. In combat, he could hypnotize with a gaze and drive creatures around him to terror and insanity just at the sight of him. His whip-like tail had the ability to drain the life of living foes, and his tentacles inflicted a withering disease that caused the living to rot away. He was also known to be extremely resistant to magic.

In addition to being worshipped by the Demon Rays known as ixitxachitls, he was also worshipped by troglodytes, kuo-toa, aboleths, merrows, scrags, and other demons. He offered pacts with Warlocks, and is credited with the creation of chimeras, ettins, and many other strange creatures of the abyss who burst their way into the material plane from time to time.

