#descr "Dagon (pr: Day-gon) was a primordial, an obyrith, and a demon lord. The Lord of the Darkened Depths laired in the Shadowsea, the 89th layer of the Abyss. Dagon was served by aquatic demons, especially wastriliths, and was worshiped by aquatic races such as kraken, chuuls, sea hags, water nagas, and kuo-toa.

In ancient myth, when the first primordials arrived in the Abyss, Dagon was already there, lurking in the depths. When Demogorgon went to claim the shard of evil, Dagon rose out of the Blood Sea to challenge him for control. Their rivalry has persisted in the eons since.

Dagon's history on Toril lay below the surface of the Sea of Fallen Stars. He and his minions lurked deep beneath the Trench of Lopok and were known by the tritons as 'Those who Sleep Below.' Dagon wished to achieve true divinity. To do so, he plotted to weaken and consume an entire pantheon of minor gods and chose the gods of the primitive Shalarin who lived in the Sea of Corynactis, near far-away Maztica. Dagon conjured ancient eldritch magic known as the 'Wild Tides' to sweep large numbers of shalarin from their homes and into the Sea of Fallen Stars, where his minions could slaughter them. The first wild tide began in −1509 DR with the opening of the Wildtider Gate near modern-day As'Arem. Many thousands of shalarin were suddenly swept into the Sea of Fallen Stars and roughly 70% were massacred in the confusion. Merfolk and tritons managed to rescue a small number, who found themselves cut off from their gods entirely. 

Dagon repeated this tactic every 720 years until the last wild tide of 1371 DR when the gate remained permanently open. The shalarin who poured into the Sea of Fallen Stars were horrificly found to have abandoned their native gods and now venerated Dagon himself. Unable to sever the connection and too fearful of revealing their shame, the Cult of Dagon took root among the shalarin and The Lord of the Darkened Depths edged closer to divinity."
